Implements #529 as the next BH-160 spatial-truth prerequisite.

- adds an internal exact gable-roof geometry solver derived only from complete Scene host metrics + exact pitch + ridge direction;
- derives ridge line, wall-support lines, outer eaves, two planar roof halves and deterministic `z_at(x,y)` queries in the canonical Scene frame;
- declared overhang extends the roof plane beyond the wall and lowers the outer eave consistently with pitch rather than moving architectural wall truth;
- a pitch range is never collapsed to a midpoint/default construction angle;
- unsupported roof types and incomplete host geometry remain explicit non-geometries;
- BH-167 chimney bearing now consumes exact roof planes when available and distinguishes `roof_plane_contact` from `roof_plane_required` and `unsupported`;
- generic behavioral tests cover both ridge orientations, support/eave elevations, interpolation, overhang, pitch-range uncertainty, unsupported types, exact chimney-plane contact, missed contact, determinism and non-mutation.

No Survey/ArchitecturalScene schema mutation and no `real-house-5` regeneration.

