## Purpose

Introduce `DASHI.Wikimedia` as a first-class native Wikimedia domain. The data/object language is represented before epistemic interpretation, and all external Wikimedia material remains governed by `Docs/SourceAttributionPolicy.md`.

This is intentionally a foundational tranche, not an autonomous Wikidata editing layer and not a claim that Wikipedia/Wikidata metadata is legal, scholarly, Indigenous-community, or DASHI theorem authority.

## Native identifiers and statement model

New:
- `DASHI/Wikimedia/IdentifierExact.agda`
- `DASHI/Wikimedia/NativeStatementExact.agda`

Typed carriers distinguish item IDs, property IDs, lexeme IDs, form IDs, and sense IDs. A QID is an external identity handle, not DASHI concept semantics.

The native statement layer retains:
- subject/entity identity;
- property identity;
- value / `someValue` / `noValue` snaks;
- rank;
- qualifiers;
- reference blocks/snaks;
- localized labels;
- sitelinks;
- content-addressable entity snapshot metadata.

Core boundaries include:
- `someValue != noValue != statement absence`;
- preferred rank is not DASHI epistemic truth;
- sitelink title is not entity identity.

## Typed source-attribution constitution

New: `DASHI/Wikimedia/SourceProvenanceExact.agda`.

`SourceLayer` distinguishes:
- Wikidata statement;
- Wikidata reference;
- Wikipedia revision;
- external referenced source;
- DASHI reconstruction;
- DASHI inference;
- DASHI theorem;
- promotion/adjudication.

This directly instantiates the repository source-attribution constitution. Provenance does not create authority; a Wikipedia sentence is not a Wikidata statement; an external datum is not a DASHI theorem.

## Concept <-> QID alignment fibre

New: `DASHI/Wikimedia/ConceptEntityAlignmentExact.agda`.

